    "name": "Home Mental Health Access Monitor",
    "description": "Integration machine that reads combined output signals from the Home Chronic Disease Monitor [2019:2023] and the Home Chronic Pain Monitor [2023:2027] to detect mental health access needs driven by chronic illness burden. Chronic disease and chronic pain are bidirectionally linked to depression and anxiety — each worsens the other — and low-income patients carrying both have the least access to mental health services. This machine identifies patients who need mental health integration into their medical home care plan. Output at [2039:2043] is available to downstream care coordination systems.",
